    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1535">

                <pb facs="1151" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/517.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Spanish Consul informs me two Spaniards of high social standing ordered to leave
                    country within five days without being informed <pb facs="1152" n="1036"
                        xml:id="pg1036"/> of cause, time expiring today. He has advised them not to
                    leave and will request Constitutionalist government if they should be arrested
                    to show cause according to law and energetically protest against such order of
                    expulsion. He requests my assistance in securing legal treatment for his
                    countrymen and, as I am convinced in the case of these two men, request
                    authority from the Department to make strong representations against arbitrary
                    expulsion of these two as well as all other foreigners in the future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
